{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChM38kCrsbbQ3XYCJGgbd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The merge is resolved and committed as `ad08ceb`, combining ticket 27's `responses` adapter with this branch's `anthropic` adapter. Typecheck, lint, the TS suite (7507/7507) and `npm run test:go` all pass. `npm run test:diff` still fails 24 of 195 checks, and the ticket's harness item stays unchecked.\n\n**The harness failures:** each one is the same gap that was already recorded for tickets 26, 27 and 36. TS adds the `__roast_continue` nudge tool to every request, and Go at `cd08f10` never does. It hits all 8 review cases on each of `chat`, `responses` and `anthropic`. Exit codes match in every scenario, and no other difference appeared, so the merge didn't add any. This needs your decision: either allowlist the nudge tool or change the TS behaviour.\n\nHow each conflict was settled:\n\n1. **Adapters:** `responses` and `anthropic` both sit in `ADAPTERS` (`src/llm/client.ts`), and `src/llm/usage.ts` has both `responsesUsage` and `anthropicUsage`.\n2. **Test helpers:** `writeInferenceStream` now writes the native stream for all three protocols. `test/helpers/review.ts` keeps both sides' helpers, and `test/index.ts` imports both sets of tests.\n3. **Harness scenarios:** I took ticket 27's naming, which adds a ` (<protocol>)` suffix to scenario names. `scenarios/m4.ts` now runs the M3 cases on `responses` and then on `anthropic`.\n4. **Allowlist:** the anthropic scenarios used to be named `review anthropic: …`. I changed the deliberate-change-21 entry in `test/diff/allowlist.ts` to match the new names (`/^review: .+ \\(anthropic\\)$/`). No `input_schema` differences got through.\n5. **Availability tests:** each branch had a test saying the other branch's protocol was missing. With all three adapters in place, the doctor roundtrip test in `test/cli/doctor.ts` now expects every protocol to pass. The construction test in `test/llm/client.ts` now expects `anthropic` to build.\n6. **Docs:** `docs/agents/llm.md` and `docs/agents/typescript.md` keep both sides' notes, with the harness notes rewritten for the combined M4 scenarios."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":345,"cache_read_input_tokens":96884,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":345},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"50db24be-f0c3-4ead-b471-086b882499cd","uuid":"7c694b5b-0f45-4e5f-a215-eebacb1b2724","timestamp":"2026-11-24T03:24:19.731Z","request_id":"req_011ChM38k3vzwNzaJdh42Mir"}
